{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0hvbGx5d29vZC8xOTk5LS1CZWZvcmUvTGF1cmVsJTIwQW5kJTIwSGFyZHklMjdzJTIwTGF1Z2hpbmclMjAyMCUyN3MlMjAlMjgxOTY1JTI5Lw","type":"movie","name":"Laurel And Hardy's Laughing 20's","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/5Pcutj7mSWCzPYjd6AJnQm54esO.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/vunCA6gcdKBhXlCfbNkHudJuIk4.jpg","description":"A compilation of primarly Laurel and Hardy shorts---From Soup to Nuts, Wrong Again, Putting the Pants on Philip, The Finishing Touch, Sugar Daddies and short clips from others---plus Max Davidson's Call of the Cuckoo and Dumb Daddies, with some cross-over Charley Chase footage, which, along with Robert Youngson's previous \"The Golden Age of Comedy\", \"When Comedy Was King\", \"Days of Thrills and Laughter\", led to a renewed interest in and a revival of television showings of Laurel and Hardy shorts. The cast was billed in order of their appearance: Oliver Hardy, Stan Laurel, Vivien Oakland (with a Vivian typo), Glen Tyron, Edna Murphy, Anita Garvin, Tiny Sanford, Jimmy Finlayson, Charlie Chase, Viola Richard, Max Davidson, Del Henderson, Josephine Crowell, Anders Randolf (as Anders Randolph), Edgar Kennedy, Dorothy Coburn, Lillian Elliott and \"Spec\" O'Donnell.\n\nReleased 17 Nov 1965 · United States of America · Language: English · 91 min\nStudio: Robert Youngson Productions\n\nOn your server — Audio: English","releaseInfo":"1965","genres":["Comedy","Hollywood"],"imdbRating":"7.8","runtime":"91 min","cast":["Jay Jackson","Stan Laurel","Oliver Hardy"],"director":["Robert Youngson"],"released":"1965-11-17T00:00:00.000Z","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Robert Youngson","character":"Director","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/847CgcWVnASr0cg7fdx80cLCrPM.jpg"},{"name":"Jay Jackson","character":"Narrator"},{"name":"Stan Laurel","character":"Stan (archive footage)","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/eT15ERUT5T3CVyf2a9JD1VAzC6q.jpg"},{"name":"Oliver Hardy","cha